<p>U.S. first lady Melania Trump presided over a United Nations Security Council meeting in New York focused on children in conflict, with an emphasis on education; the session was titled “Children, Technology and Education in Conflict”. Several outlets noted it took place as the United States and Israel continued military operations against Iran, and Trump acknowledged the difficult timing. The meeting was scheduled before the latest escalation, but it drew extra attention after Iranian state media reported a deadly strike on a girls’ school in southern Iran days earlier. In her remarks, Trump urged member states to protect children’s access to education, presenting it as a practical area where diplomacy can still secure shared safeguards even amid intensifying conflict.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ixMj9YcrmF1h3neVfy_ovgiiuTUGxVvQOv-Ostnkiy8UvLzIaKViP0kco_PrR2FXnnnG6EqhsJxiWNQBExRC67g9mI-jBjKs-LGPbJUp-SuT1BSWFwXxaUzZEU7DtqJobUFaOLcap02LhW7jBg0Jepjm7BaFfj8pP6Lgi8s2rgfJjDqMgCoY27iKw3ss34F1QosteElHWP0DHcJmR9ycEy9XuwnL3eO7kU7XjUVjKXt4r3HTort6ABcoYNOm9yeTbC7LB7oHNHFMXZx1rw' alt='Melania Trump presides over a UN Security Council meeting at UN headquarters on March 2, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Rare role: According to The Globe and Mail and The Guardian, this was the first time the spouse of a serving world leader chaired a meeting of the 15-member Security Council.</li><li>Protocol moment: Delegates addressed her as “madam president” as she led the session; she also thanked Britain for its month-long presidency of the Security Council.</li><li>Advance notice: CBS News said the White House announced ahead of time that she would preside, and that announcement came before the joint U.S.-Israeli mission in Iran began.</li><li>Acknowledged losses: The Straits Times reported that Melania Trump honoured U.S. service members killed in the war on Iran.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Melania Trump: She cast the session as a call for member states to protect children’s education, while noting she was chairing at “challenging times” as U.S.-Israel attacks on Iran continued. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-first-lady-melania-trump-presides-over-un-security-council-as-u-s-israel-attacks-on-iran-continue'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>White House (U.S.): The White House said in advance that the first lady would preside over the Security Council meeting; that announcement came before the U.S. and Israel launched a joint military mission in Iran. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/melania-trump-un-security-council-world-peace-iran/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Iranian state media (as cited): Iranian state media said an airstrike hit a girls’ school in southern Iran, shaping attention around the UN discussion on children and education. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/02/melania-trump-un-children-iran-airstrike'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/melania-trump-un-security-council-world-peace-iran/'>Melania Trump presides over U.N. Security Council meeting</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/3/melania-trump-chairs-un-meeting-on-children-days-after-iran-school-strike'>Melania Trump chairs UN meeting on children days after Iran school strike</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-melania-trump-un-united-nations/'>U.S. first lady Melania Trump chairs UN meeting on children in conflict</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-first-lady-melania-trump-presides-over-un-security-council-as-u-s-israel-attacks-on-iran-continue'>WATCH: First lady Melania Trump presides over UN Security Council as U.S.-Israel attacks on Iran continue</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/02/melania-trump-un-children-iran-airstrike'>Melania Trump urges protecting children’s education at 